 > **v2.12.0 in one line:** at L3 the second signal beyond tests and Codex is no longer a GLM read of finished code but **guard-break evidence** — each safety guard broken on purpose and a test shown to catch it (`attest --mutation`); GLM reviews the plan before code and is printed as advisory. Measurements: `docs/DESIGN-NOTE-v2.12.md`.
 > **v2.11.0 kept:** the SessionStart hook is three lines of invariants instead of six kilobytes of process — enforcement lives in `coverloop gate`, where it is fail-closed, and what stays in prose is a pointer at it plus the rules no command enforces. `classify`, `attest` and `gate` are unchanged. **v2.10.9 kept:** `coverloop classify` turns the risk tier from a declaration into a **derived floor** — migrations, auth/RLS, money, secrets, CI/deploy and workers are L3 by path, unrecognised files are L1 (never L0), and nothing may lower a deterministic floor. **v2.9.0 kept:** every response that ends with a next task now closes with a one-line **model + effort recommendation** for that task (§9b) — so the operator never burns a frontier model on a mechanical job, nor a cheap one on an L3. **v2.7.3 kept:** a full multi-lineage audit (Claude + real GPT-5.6 Sol + real GLM, every finding adversarially verified) closed 4 P1s and hardened the rest — no P0s: a laundered failed-capture forge (withheld-marker check now source-agnostic), the `_KEY` secret-family the filter missed, an untracked-file fail-open in the Stop hook, and an honestly-labeled `--require-executed` ceiling; plus symlink-safe evidence writes, monotonic tier floors, an opt-in `--require-clean-tree`, and shape-guarded reports. **v2.7.2 kept:** off-policy review + Sol effort routing (high L2 / xhigh L3 / max deadlock, never ultra) + PII redaction. v2.7 kept: the fail-closed commit-bound gate as a required CI check.
 > **MODEL_ROSTER_LAST_VERIFIED: 2026-09-23** (plan reviewer switched to Kimi K3 — `glm-review --zdr-selftest` OK, served via a ZDR endpoint with fallbacks off; earlier: GLM full-ZDR re-verified 2026-07-02 on both VPS users; M3 `data_collection:deny` verified 2026-06-28, enabled for your-vps-user + your-vps-user) — endpoint availability on these dates, not a permanent fact. Re-verify with `glm-review --zdr-selftest` / `m3-review --privacy-selftest` when reusing later.
