 ### GLM-5.2 — architecture red-team of the plan (PRE; POST retired as a gate in v2.12)
 - **GLM-PRE** (`glm-redteam` / `glm-redteam-xhigh`) — runs on the DESIGN PACKET *before* any implementation code. Exit criterion: zero unresolved P0/P1 design findings; design packet frozen (Section 5).
 - **GLM-POST — retired as a gate (v2.12).** Measured across the fleet it failed operationally on roughly one run in five and its adjudicated P0/P1 findings were mostly false positives from code outside the packet (`docs/DESIGN-NOTE-v2.12.md`). What it was meant to prove on finished code — every invariant holds, no fallback reintroduces the bug — is now shown by **guard-break evidence**: each safety guard broken on purpose, a test shown to fail (`coverloop attest --mutation pass --mutation-guards N --mutation-log <file>`, N ≥ 1). A GLM diff review may still be run and recorded; the gate prints it as advisory and it never changes the verdict.
+- **`glm-diff-review` — advisory review of finished code (v2.12.5).** At L3, after tests and before Codex, run it twice in parallel on the diff plus the files it touches: `glm-diff-review "<task>" < packet &` and `GLM_MODEL=moonshotai/kimi-k3.1-pro REVIEWER_NAME="Kimi K3.1" glm-diff-review "<task>" < packet &`, then `wait`. Optional below L3 (one K3 run). Every finding is a claim to verify; no findings proves nothing; a failed run is noted and does not block. The secret filter applies as always: if it refuses a packet (exit 3), send the diff with narrower excerpts; never weaken the filter. It is not a gate.
 - **Execute before review; two-round rule.** Build, tests and guard-break run BEFORE the diff goes to Codex. If a P1 is still open after two Codex rounds, stop and redesign — the measured 7–16-round tails were design errors found late.
 
 GLM owns **INVARIANT and CROSS-FILE safety** — money/auth/migration invariant preservation, race conditions, deploy-order, a fallback reintroducing the original bug, whole-subsystem consistency — scoped beyond the diff. Not an authority; each finding classified per Section 6.
