   281	    Two ways the old `--name-only` + splitlines() collection lost paths, and both
   282	    are classifier EVASION, not cosmetics:
   283	
   284	      * rename detection reported only the DESTINATION, so moving
   285	        src/authGuard.ts to src/guard.ts made an auth change look like an
   286	        unrecognised source file. `--no-renames` reports both sides.
   287	      * git C-quotes any name containing a newline or tab, and splitlines() then
   288	        tore that single path into two meaningless fragments. `-z` emits raw
   289	        names separated by NUL, so there is nothing to quote and nothing to tear.
   290	    """
   291	    # `--no-renames` is a diff option; ls-files rejects it, and appending it
   292	    # blindly made every collection return None — which the caller then, quite
   293	    # correctly, read as "cannot determine the paths" and held at L1. Correct
   294	    # fail-closed behaviour, wrong cause, and it would have masked the evasion
   295	    # fix it was meant to deliver.
   296	    # `show` takes diff options too, and it defaults to rename detection just
   297	    # like `diff` — scoping the flag to `diff` alone let the root-commit fallback
   298	    # lose a rename origin again, one commit after that hole was closed.
   299	    # `ls-files` is the only caller here that rejects it.
