     2	
     3	> **PROTOCOL_VERSION: v2.12.5** (`glm-diff-review`: a sharper advisory review of a finished change, run on K3 and K3.1 at L3; v2.12.4: the floor's baseline walk has no 100-report cap — it stops at the newest valid L3 anchor; v2.12.3: a recorded exit_code must be a real integer; v2.12.2: a failed reviewer run is never a pass — saved, inherited or gated; v2.12.1: guard-break pass must state its guard count, plan reviewer → Kimi K3) · **CONTRACT_VERSION: v2.10** (the Operating Contract block inlined in each project's `CLAUDE.md`; bumps only when the contract's CONTENT changes — see §13. **v2.10: the plan reviewer is Kimi K3 and a guard-break pass states its guard count. v2.9: guard-break evidence is mandatory at L3, GLM moves to reviewing the plan before L3 code, execute before review, and the two-round rule.** v2.5 made it version-agnostic; v2.6 added GPT-5.6 Sol + per-tier effort routing and the off-policy review rule; v2.7 added §9b (next-task model + effort recommendation); **v2.8 adds §2a — the risk tier is no longer self-declared: `coverloop classify` derives a deterministic floor from the changed paths and the gate takes the MAX**, so it triggers a one-time fleet contract resync). History: [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md).
     4	> **v2.12.0 in one line:** at L3 the second signal beyond tests and Codex is no longer a GLM read of finished code but **guard-break evidence** — each safety guard broken on purpose and a test shown to catch it (`attest --mutation`); GLM reviews the plan before code and is printed as advisory. Measurements: `docs/DESIGN-NOTE-v2.12.md`.
   425	
   426	## 13. Versioning & Sync
   427	
   428	**Two versions, decoupled (v2.5).** `PROTOCOL_VERSION` (this doc + tooling) bumps freely; **`CONTRACT_VERSION`** (the Operating Contract block inlined in every project's `CLAUDE.md` — this doc's header declares **v2.11**, while the distributable template `docs/OPERATING_CONTRACT.md`, which `init-project.sh` copies into new projects, is a **v2.6 base carrying the v2.9–v2.11 L3 evidence and roster rows** (guard-break, GLM plan review, execute-before-review, two-round rule) and still lacking the v2.7–v2.8 content (§9b model line, §2a derived floor); resyncing it is a separate change) bumps ONLY when the contract's content changes. Why: the contract is the *expensive-to-sync* artifact (a PR per project), while machines resync with one `git pull && ./install.sh`. So a docs/tooling release costs the fleet nothing; only a genuine contract change triggers per-project resyncs. `protocol-selftest` cross-checks all of it (the installed hook file vs the repo's = must match — the shortened hook prints no version banner to compare; project contract vs `CONTRACT_VERSION` = warn on drift). Each CLI prints `FILTER_VERSION`/`CLI_VERSION` on `--version`; copies are installed FROM the repo, never edited in place; a filter-version mismatch between machines is a STOP for cross-machine work. When the protocol changes, bump the right version and update `CHANGELOG.md` in the same commit.
   429	
     1	#!/bin/sh
     2	# A diff packet carries the change plus the files it touches, and thinking through it takes minutes:
     3	# measured 2-6 min on 130-155 KB packets, past the helper's default 120 s and 120000 chars.
     4	DIR="$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")" && pwd)"
     5	GLM_TIMEOUT=600 GLM_MAX_CHARS=200000 GLM_MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS=24000 \
     6	exec "$DIR/glm-review" --mode diff "$@"

