.coverloop/reports/694e9cb1d5892d133df1376dc4a5ae7a1f6c9e49.codex.log:15:Independent diff review. The prior review raised one P1: three callers still collected pathnames line-by-line, so the path-normalisation bypass survived in only_evidence_changed(), changed_files(), and --require-clean-tree. This diff routes all three through _git_paths() (raw NUL parsing) and adds a structural test that fails if any pathname-producing git call sits outside it. Verify the fix is correct and complete, and check nothing broke in those three callers' semantics (None handling, empty results, artifact filtering). Be decisive: if there is no genuine fail-open, say PASS. End with exactly: VERDICT: PASS or VERDICT: ISSUES
.coverloop/reports/694e9cb1d5892d133df1376dc4a5ae7a1f6c9e49.codex.log:510:- **Codex CLI** = mandatory independent code/diff reviewer for meaningful PRs.
